WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Connect it to Claude Code and Claude Desktop.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.128
A host connects to a stdio server by running the command that starts it.

3
00:00:07.408 --> 00:00:09.883
Everything else is where you write that command.

4
00:00:10.163 --> 00:00:13.683
Claude Code registers servers with claude mcp add.

5
00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:27.253
Options come first, then a name, then two dashes, then the launch command: claude mcp add harbor -- /absolute/path/to/python /absolute/path/to/server.

6
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:28.280
py.

7
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:38.160
Add --env KEY=value for credentials and --scope for where the entry lives: local (the default, only you in this project), project (a.

8
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.443
mcp.

9
00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:46.997
json file you commit for your team, which Claude Code asks each person to approve), or user (all your projects).

10
00:00:47.277 --> 00:00:51.523
Inside a session, /mcp shows status and lets you reconnect.

11
00:00:51.803 --> 00:01:01.253
Each tool appears as mcp__harbor__get_issue, the same name you use in permission rules, so you can allow the read tools and keep the write tool on “ask.

12
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:18.472
” Claude Code also warns when a tool’s output passes 10,000 tokens and caps it at 25,000 by default (adjustable with MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS ), a concrete reason to return summaries and paginate.

13
00:01:18.752 --> 00:01:21.525
Claude Desktop reads a claude_desktop_config.

14
00:01:21.805 --> 00:01:32.899
json file (on macOS under ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/ ) with an mcpServers entry holding the command and arguments.

15
00:01:33.179 --> 00:01:35.909
The SDK’s mcp install server.

16
00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:40.584
py can write the entry for a file that defines a module-level server.

17
00:01:40.864 --> 00:01:43.381
Fully quit and reopen the app after editing.

18
00:01:43.661 --> 00:01:46.200
Its per-server logs, mcp-server-NAME.

19
00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:51.088
log, are under ~/Library/Logs/Claude on macOS.

20
00:01:51.368 --> 00:01:57.000
When a server does not show up, the SDK docs suggest running the launch command yourself first.

21
00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.949
A healthy stdio server prints nothing and waits for input.

22
00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:09.421
Then check the three usual causes: a relative path, a host still running its old configuration, or something writing to stdout.
